{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records as Segment-spec track calls to Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Segment, RudderStack and Customer.io Data Pipelines each take the same batch call of the Segment","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spec, at endpoints of their own. One encoder, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":", writes it, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factory for each fills in the endpoint and how the key travels:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" posts to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"type":"text","text":" of the workspace’s region ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), with the write key as HTTP Basic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authentication’s user name and an empty password."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" posts to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of your data plane URL, with the write key the same way.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" posts to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Pipelines API’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"type":"text","text":" in the workspace’s region ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion"},{"type":"text","text":"), with the key as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bearer token and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X-Strict-Mode: 1"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each splits a batch to the spec’s limits (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference"},{"text":"): 2,500 calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and 500 KB a request, and under 32 KB a call, which all three accept. A batch with no record the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. Each retries no response, a 5xx, 408","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The key goes in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization"},{"type":"text","text":" header field, never in the body. It is a public client key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Segment’s and RudderStack’s write keys, and Customer.io’s public keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pk_…"},{"type":"text","text":"), ship in their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendors’ own app and web libraries, and they let a client send data to the source and read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s private keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sk_…"},{"type":"text","text":") reach every Customer.io API, deleting people included, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factory throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/privateKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for one. Each factory throws for an empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), RudderStack’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a data plane URL that isn’t a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":" URL, and Customer.io’s for a public key of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other region."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A region has no default. Segment and Customer.io keep a workspace’s data in the US or the EU, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events posted to the other region’s endpoint don’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes a track call of an anonymous user. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the sessions enricher; a record with no session is sent under its own record identifier. No"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":" call or traits are sent. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a redelivered record keeps, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. The standard context"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"goes in the spec’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"},{"type":"text","text":" fields ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os"},{"type":"text","text":"), with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device.id"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"advertisingId"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Segment takes in place of the request’s address, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it records none. RudderStack fills in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the request unless the call has one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"even beside ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and passes it on to its destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Customer.io’s references don’t say whether ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes the place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the address it reads from an HTTP request, so it may still record the request’s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each endpoint counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is each record sent without a session. On a plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out under the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. Segment deduplicates calls by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops most duplicates within about 24 hours, not all, so one it stored before the app ended is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most likely not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s API references don’t say whether"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they deduplicate, so such a record may be stored twice there."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one named as one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices (","type":"text"},{"code":"User Deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"User Suppressed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Device Deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest), one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for a call. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":", and the encoder logs a notice for each semantic event name in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan when the destination is made.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Segment answers 200 for every request but one too large or not JSON, so a wrong region, a write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key of no source, or a batch of more calls than it takes may be answered 200 with nothing stored.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Check the source’s debugger after setting the destination up. RudderStack answers a wrong write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key with 401, and Customer.io, in strict mode, with 401 too, so the destination reports those. In","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"strict mode Customer.io refuses a whole batch for one bad call, so the encoder leaves out each call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io documents refusing; a 400 for anything else drops the whole request.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude or Mixpanel, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SegmentSpecEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: segment)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what each endpoint receives, and why, in more detail."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"SegmentSpecEncoding","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding"]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Segment","anchor":"Sending-to-Segment"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"],"title":"Sending to RudderStack","anchor":"Sending-to-RudderStack"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Customer.io Data Pipelines","anchor":"Sending-to-Customerio-Data-Pipelines"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/Segme